On 6 Aug 2003, Dr Darth wrote:

> My Cha Wiz was just starting out on his journey.  He killed a
> homonculous and sacrificed it on the first altar that he found, and
> got the message "You feel partially absolved".  I've never seen this
> before - what is it?  It sounds as though my god was angry, but my
> next sacrifice (a garter snake corpse) was completely normal (ie I
> didn't get a feeling of inadequacy).  What's going on?

You had a negative alignment, but your god was not angry with you. In
this situation, a successful sacrifice will adjust your alignment and
produce the message "You feel partially absolved.". In your case, the
maximum value of 0 was reached.

A feeling of inadequacy can only occur if the god is angry with you (if
you have killed your pet or sacrificed something of your own race, for
example).

